WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.611
Good morning, it's Thursday, November 26.

00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:09.363
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:18.470
Today: Black Friday tests shopping agents at checkout, Cloudera launches a sovereignty offer, and Claude Ship bills even in observe-only mode.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.317
First, the story of the day.

00:00:20.381 --> 00:00:30.826
TechCrunch reports that Walmart now lets shoppers buy its Black Friday deals through Meta's Muse, and plans to open its gateway to more developers and AI platforms.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:37.705
TechCrunch also says Amazon has taken steps to stop third-party agents from making purchases for customers.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:46.940
TechTarget notes that agents already show up on retail sites, but that nobody has documented large numbers of them shopping for a single person.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.786
The bigger picture: you now have two public postures to compare.

00:00:51.852 --> 00:00:55.236
Walmart builds a dedicated door and sets the terms.

00:00:55.302 --> 00:00:56.231
Amazon blocks.

00:00:56.297 --> 00:01:02.136
Most retailers sit in between, and by default that means whatever your bot rules decide.

00:01:02.202 --> 00:01:13.746
So check what your bot protection does with a legitimate agent, whether a blocked agent gets a clear answer, and whether you can tell agent orders from human ones afterwards.

00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:18.058
Black Friday traffic will likely be noisy and hard to attribute.

00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:20.380
Still, treat it as free test data.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:24.560
Log it, and write down your posture before the January review.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.007
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:01:27.071 --> 00:01:35.989
Cloudera announced Cloudera for Digital Sovereignty on November twenty-fourth at its EVOLVE event in Madrid, according to Compare the Cloud.

00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:43.825
It lets organisations run governed data and private AI across sovereign clouds, private data centres and air-gapped sites.

00:01:43.889 --> 00:01:50.323
It builds on support for the AWS European Sovereign Cloud and on Cloudera's partnership with Mistral.

00:01:50.386 --> 00:01:52.170
The source gives no pricing.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:59.860
Reading between the lines: data platforms are repositioning as the control layer across mixed estates.

00:01:59.929 --> 00:02:02.223
The claim to test is portability.

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:07.505
Can retrieval, lineage and policy move between environments without rework?

00:02:07.575 --> 00:02:12.440
Ask for named regions and operators before calling anything sovereign.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:13.993
Next, Platform.

00:02:14.057 --> 00:02:19.521
Claude Ship, from Anthropic, is billed on token usage, according to Help Net Security.

00:02:19.584 --> 00:02:25.366
Claude Approvals has no base charge, but the classifiers in a policy consume billed tokens.

00:02:25.429 --> 00:02:31.529
Policies that rely on Claude's review trigger a billable Code Review, even in observe-only mode.

00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:38.200
Eligible Enterprise customers can claim at least ten thousand dollars in credits, valid for thirty days.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.599
Why it matters: observe-only is not free.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:46.787
The trial that compares agent verdicts with human ones still spends tokens.

00:02:46.856 --> 00:02:52.590
Set the monthly cap before you start, and meter cost per merged change from day one.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.293
Next, Regulation.

00:02:54.358 --> 00:02:59.353
The Commission proposed the Cloud and AI Development Act on June third, 2026.

00:02:59.418 --> 00:03:07.592
According to a Qovery analysis, it covers four Union assurance levels, public procurement minimums and data centre permitting.

00:03:07.657 --> 00:03:14.404
The Irish Council presidency tabled a first compromise text on the sovereignty pillar on November tenth.

00:03:14.469 --> 00:03:19.659
Parliament's co-rapporteurs presented a joint draft report on November eleventh.

00:03:19.724 --> 00:03:21.800
The act is still in negotiation.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.307
The bigger picture: nothing binds you yet.

00:03:25.376 --> 00:03:30.914
But the assurance levels will likely become the vocabulary of sovereign tenders.

00:03:30.983 --> 00:03:34.998
Worth watching whether the Council's softer text survives.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:41.020
For now, classify your workloads by sensitivity, so you can map them to a level later.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.017
The number of the day.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.811
One hundred fifty-seven point five percent.

00:03:45.874 --> 00:03:54.001
That is the rise in AI-agent requests from September to October across applications protected by Human Security, per TechTarget.

00:03:54.065 --> 00:03:59.271
It counts requests, not shoppers or sales, so size bot rules with it, not revenue.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:00.223
What to watch.

00:04:00.287 --> 00:04:08.350
Black Friday, November twenty-seventh, then Cyber Monday on November thirtieth, as a first test of shopping agents at checkout.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:11.017
Which agents Walmart admits next to Muse.

00:04:11.081 --> 00:04:14.954
Whether Claude Ship's beta agents reach general availability.

00:04:15.017 --> 00:04:18.509
Prices, quotas and regions for OVHcloud's new products.

00:04:18.573 --> 00:04:30.192
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:04:30.256 --> 00:04:32.097
And a question for your team.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:40.986
When a shopping agent hits your site this weekend, can your logs show whether it was blocked, served or ordered, and who decided that rule?

00:04:41.049 --> 00:04:42.319
That's it for today.

00:04:42.383 --> 00:04:44.859
Sources are in the episode description.

00:04:44.922 --> 00:04:46.827
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:04:46.891 --> 00:04:47.970
See you tomorrow.
